<title>USA: White House seeks NTSB accident investigation fees.</title>
<headline>White House seeks NTSB accident investigation fees.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The White House Thursday called for a new fee to offset part of the National Transportation Safety Board's &quot;growing cost&quot; of commercial aviation accident investigations.</p>
<p>In its fiscal 1998 budget plan, the administration proposed that commercial air carriers pay fees to cover aviation recoveries and investigations, based on their revenue flight hours of operation.</p>
<p>The fee would collect an estimated $6 million in 1998, the budget plan said.</p>
</text>
